# What sources/hidden.lua needs from outside Hammerspoon, declared beside the only file that
# builds and filters the hidden index.
# Format is name | kind | locator | policy | reason.
# See Dependencies.spoon for the kinds and for how these files are found.
#
# Two tools rather than one, and they do different jobs. The walker builds the index, which is
# the complement of what Spotlight holds, and the finder filters it. The walker is declared
# here as well as beside walk.lua, because a declaration belongs beside whatever knows the tool
# and neither file should have to learn that the other exists. The manifest carries a line per
# owner and the reconciler joins on the name, so one map entry answers both.
#
# Both optional. Without them, unscoped hidden search is the one thing that stops working and
# it says so, while a scoped hidden search still answers through the walk source and every
# ordinary search still answers through Spotlight.
fd | path | fd | optional | building the index of paths Spotlight cannot see
fzf | path | fzf | optional | ranking that index, the one thing a substring tool cannot do over 42 thousand matches
